---
// 3.1: the same order lines as one wide flat table, and as a star schema. The flat table repeats product and
// store details on every line; the star keeps each fact once.
---
<figure class="cs-fig pbi">
  <span class="cs-figtag">Flat table or star?</span>
  <div class="pbi-two">
    <div class="pbi-tv"><p class="pbi-tvname">One flat table</p><div class="pbi-tablewrap"><table class="pbi-mini"><thead><tr><th>Date</th><th class="hi">Product</th><th class="hi">Category</th><th class="hi">Store</th><th class="hi">Region</th><th>Qty</th><th>Amount</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td>2025-03-01</td><td class="hi">Desk lamp</td><td class="hi">Home</td><td class="hi">Rideau</td><td class="hi">East</td><td>2</td><td>79.04</td></tr>
      <tr><td>2025-03-01</td><td class="hi">Desk lamp</td><td class="hi">Home</td><td class="hi">Queen Street</td><td class="hi">Central</td><td>1</td><td>39.52</td></tr>
      <tr><td>2025-03-02</td><td class="hi">Desk lamp</td><td class="hi">Home</td><td class="hi">Rideau</td><td class="hi">East</td><td>1</td><td>39.52</td></tr>
      <tr><td>2025-03-02</td><td class="hi">Smart plug</td><td class="hi">Electronics</td><td class="hi">Rideau</td><td class="hi">East</td><td>3</td><td>93.60</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></div><p class="pbi-tvfoot">Highlighted text repeats on every line: 7,000+ times "Desk lamp", "Home", "Rideau", "East"…</p></div>
    <div class="pbi-tv"><p class="pbi-tvname">Star schema</p><div class="pbi-tablewrap"><table class="pbi-mini"><thead><tr><th>Date</th><th>ProductKey</th><th>StoreKey</th><th>Qty</th><th>Amount</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td>2025-03-01</td><td>5</td><td>4</td><td>2</td><td>79.04</td></tr><tr><td>2025-03-01</td><td>5</td><td>3</td><td>1</td><td>39.52</td></tr><tr><td>2025-03-02</td><td>5</td><td>4</td><td>1</td><td>39.52</td></tr><tr><td>2025-03-02</td><td>9</td><td>4</td><td>3</td><td>93.60</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></div><p class="pbi-tvfoot">Sales keeps only keys and numbers. "Desk lamp, Home" lives once, in Product; "Rideau, East" once, in Store.</p></div>
  </div>
  <figcaption>Both hold the same facts. The star is smaller, a change of category name is made in one row instead of thousands, and every dimension can filter every fact table. Power BI's engine is built for stars.</figcaption>
</figure>
